        "note.002.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.002.source.start" "384"
        "note.002.source.end" "406"
        "note.003.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.003.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.001.text" "Hybrid combat-role mapping (D26): from `creatures.json` `role` text, take the first matching"
        "note.003.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.002.text" "keyword in priority order **any-class / ranged / mage / melee**. Absent text or no matching"
        "note.003.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.003.text" "keyword leaves the role unset, distinct from the listed `none` value; spawn resolution follows §6 `gen-spawns`."
        "note.003.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.003.source.start" "408"
        "note.003.source.end" "410"
        "note.004.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.004.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.004.line.001.text" "A Snout Beetle charged shot's model must **not continuously grow to fill the screen**;"
        "note.004.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.004.line.002.text" "this bug grants no growing damage or new attack behavior. Existing combat and encounters stand;"
        "note.004.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.004.line.003.text" "D26 combat-role species overrides grant no exception."
        "note.004.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.004.source.start" "412"
        "note.004.source.end" "414"
        "note.005.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.005.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.005.line.001.text" "Hybrid ordinary Lion (`lion`): **untameable**, retaining hostile jungle/savannah encounters."
        "note.005.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.005.line.002.text" "Snow Lions and other cats are unchanged; this selects no food pairing or riding permission."
        "note.005.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.005.source.start" "416"
        "note.005.source.end" "417"
        "note.006.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.006.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.006.line.001.text" "Source IDs (reconciliation item 6, approved 2026-09-15): the cuwo alpha reference table covers"
        "note.006.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.006.line.002.text" "0..155; post-alpha additions may have larger IDs. Radishling Sprout / Mineral Water share 192,"
        "note.006.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.006.line.003.text" "and Caterpillar / Mixed Salad share 293 (`research/research_creatures_quests.md §2.5`)."
        "note.006.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.006.line.004.text" "Version tags, not the integer alone, record provenance: an alpha-reserved ID does not prove"
        "note.006.line.005.state" "text"
        "note.006.line.005.text" "alpha availability (F10). Preserve stable creature IDs, numeric source IDs, version tags and"
        "note.006.line.006.state" "text"
        "note.006.line.006.text" "`tame-food` / `pet-food.tames` pairings. Keep the legacy field names for compatibility; do not"
        "note.006.line.007.state" "text"
        "note.006.line.007.text" "clamp later IDs to the alpha range or invent values for unrecorded IDs."
        "note.006.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.006.source.start" "419"
        "note.006.source.end" "425"
    }
}

r_creature_family = element "creature-family" "Class" {
    tags "Class,Entities"
    properties {
        "id" "creature-family"
        "kind" "Class"
        "order" "427"
        "source.commit" "175e0c59b6a05ead62d29bd851085cd5a3818378"
        "source.status" "historical baseline coordinates"
        "source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "source.start" "427"
        "source.end" "512"
        "title" "creature-family"
        "heading.level" "3"
        "heading.slug" "creature-family"
        "section" "Entities"
        "note.001.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.001.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.001.text" "Shared base form. → `instances/creature-families.json` (top-level family `members` lists,"
        "note.001.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.002.text" "not nested spawn rosters). These taxonomy records follow §5 Validation-contract mapping item 1."
        "note.001.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.001.source.start" "428"
        "note.001.source.end" "429"
        "note.002.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.002.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.001.text" "**Hybrid family item 1 (owner approved with amendment, 2026-09-27):** a creature has at most"
        "note.002.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.002.text" "one primary balancing family (`family` / `member-of-family`). Multiple descriptive memberships"
        "note.002.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.003.text" "(`descriptive-families` / `descriptive-member-of-family`) may coexist, but never supply or stack"
        "note.002.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.004.text" "family stat modifiers. Top-level family `members` lists describe memberships, not multiple"
        "note.002.line.005.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.005.text" "primary assignments or automatic species-trait inheritance."
        "note.002.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.002.source.start" "431"
        "note.002.source.end" "435"
        "note.003.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.003.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.001.text" "**Skeleton Dog (`skeleton-dog`) has primary family `dogs`, not `skeletons`.** It retains descriptive"
        "note.003.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.002.text" "membership in both dogs and skeletons; its `undead` category is independent and unchanged."
        "note.003.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.003.text" "Other existing primary assignments remain. The family assignment itself changes no taming,"
        "note.003.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.004.text" "abilities, drops, hostility, habitats or pack aggro, and introduces no numerical family modifier."
        "note.003.line.005.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.005.text" "Items 4–6 below separately decide encounter rarity and extend variant habitat permission,"
        "note.003.line.006.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.006.text" "not combat/loot tiers."
        "note.003.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.003.source.start" "437"
        "note.003.source.end" "442"
        "note.004.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.004.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.004.line.001.text" "Documentation only: live `creatures.json` still assigns Skeleton Dog to `skeletons`; migration,"
        "note.004.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.004.line.002.text" "model/loader/validator support and runtime family scaling remain deferred and unauthorized."
        "note.004.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.004.line.003.text" "There is no live family `hp-mult` data or runtime family scaling today."
        "note.004.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.004.source.start" "444"
        "note.004.source.end" "446"
        "note.005.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.005.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.005.line.001.text" "**Hybrid family item 2 (owner approved, 2026-09-27):** these 25 missing primary assignments"
        "note.005.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.005.line.002.text" "are authoritative. Preserve all other existing assignments except item 1's Skeleton Dog override."
        "note.005.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.005.line.003.text" "No numerical changes, new family classifications or species-trait inheritance are introduced."
        "note.005.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.005.line.004.text" "Live JSON still lacks these assignments; migration remains deferred."
        "note.005.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.005.source.start" "448"
        "note.005.source.end" "451"
        "note.006.kind" "table"
        "note.006.column.001.text" "primary family"
        "note.006.column.002.text" "creature IDs"
        "note.006.row.001.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.006.row.001.source.start" "455"
        "note.006.row.001.source.end" "455"
        "note.006.row.001.cell.001.state" "text"
        "note.006.row.001.cell.001.text" "cats (3)"
        "note.006.row.001.cell.002.state" "text"
        "note.006.row.001.cell.002.text" "`cat`, `brown-cat`, `white-cat`"
        "note.006.row.002.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.006.row.002.source.start" "456"
        "note.006.row.002.source.end" "456"
        "note.006.row.002.cell.001.state" "text"
        "note.006.row.002.cell.001.text" "sprouts (9)"
        "note.006.row.002.cell.002.state" "text"
        "note.006.row.002.cell.002.text" "`onionling`, `desert-onionling`, `radishling`, `radishling-sprout`, `cormling`, `cormling-sprout`, `chiling`, `habanero`, `bloomling`"
        "note.006.row.003.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.006.row.003.source.start" "457"
        "note.006.row.003.source.end" "457"
        "note.006.row.003.cell.001.state" "text"
        "note.006.row.003.cell.001.text" "guardians (2)"
        "note.006.row.003.cell.002.state" "text"
        "note.006.row.003.cell.002.text" "`ancient-guardian-anubis`, `ancient-guardian-horus`"
        "note.006.row.004.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.006.row.004.source.start" "458"
        "note.006.row.004.source.end" "458"
        "note.006.row.004.cell.001.state" "text"
        "note.006.row.004.cell.001.text" "trolls (3)"
        "note.006.row.004.cell.002.state" "text"
        "note.006.row.004.cell.002.text" "`troll`, `dark-troll`, `yeti`"
        "note.006.row.005.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.006.row.005.source.start" "459"
        "note.006.row.005.source.end" "459"
        "note.006.row.005.cell.001.state" "text"
        "note.006.row.005.cell.001.text" "fish (8)"
        "note.006.row.005.cell.002.state" "text"
        "note.006.row.005.cell.002.text" "`sapphire-fish`, `lemon-fish`, `seahorse`, `shark`, `lantern-fish`, `maw-fish`, `piranha`, `blowfish`"
        "note.006.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.006.source.start" "453"
        "note.006.source.end" "459"
        "note.007.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.007.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.007.line.001.text" "**Hybrid family item 3 (owner approved, 2026-09-27):** creatures outside the defined families"
        "note.007.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.007.line.002.text" "may remain unassigned. With no primary family, the family modifier is **×1.0**, preserving all"
        "note.007.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.007.line.003.text" "other ordinary stat calculations (`design.enemy-hp` already records this default). Do not invent"
        "note.007.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.007.line.004.text" "catch-all families merely to fill every entry."
        "note.007.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.007.source.start" "461"
        "note.007.source.end" "464"
        "note.008.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.008.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.008.line.001.text" "**Hybrid family item 4 (owner approved with amendment, 2026-09-27):** Skeleton Dog has a"
        "note.008.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.008.line.002.text" "**1% encounter chance relative to dog spawns**; the remaining 99% are non-skeletal dogs."
        "note.008.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.008.line.003.text" "This replaces the proposed one-tenth relative species-selection weight. The denominator is dog"
        "note.008.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.008.line.004.text" "spawns, not all creatures, and 1% is a probability, not a guaranteed quota every 100 encounters."
        "note.008.line.005.state" "text"
        "note.008.line.005.text" "It grants no extra combat strength or loot tier."
        "note.008.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.008.source.start" "466"
        "note.008.source.end" "470"
        "note.009.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.009.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.009.line.001.text" "**Hybrid family item 5 (owner approved, 2026-09-27):** roll the 1% chance independently for"
        "note.009.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.009.line.002.text" "**each individual dog**, not once per pack. Packs may mix ordinary and skeletal dogs. The"
        "note.009.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.009.line.003.text" "denominator remains dog spawns, with no per-species weighting or guaranteed quota."
        "note.009.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.009.source.start" "472"
        "note.009.source.end" "474"
        "note.010.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.010.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.010.line.001.text" "**Hybrid family item 6 (owner approved, 2026-09-27):** apply the rare dog variant **wherever"
        "note.010.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.010.line.002.text" "dogs already spawn**, not only Skeleton Dog's former dungeons/dark woods/deadlands habitats."
        "note.010.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.010.line.003.text" "Preserve existing settlement safety (`c-hostile-in-city`); this does not make protected town"
        "note.010.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.010.line.004.text" "inhabitants attackable. This habitat permission itself changes no species' abilities, taming, drops,"
        "note.010.line.005.state" "text"
        "note.010.line.005.text" "hostility, combat/loot tiers or pack aggro; item 7 separately amends Skeleton Dog's temperament"
        "note.010.line.006.state" "text"
        "note.010.line.006.text" "and tameability."
        "note.010.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.010.source.start" "476"
        "note.010.source.end" "481"
        "note.011.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.011.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.011.line.001.text" "**Hybrid family item 7 (owner approved with amendment, 2026-09-27):** use **Collie (`collie`)**"
        "note.011.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.011.line.002.text" "for ordinary outcomes wherever an already-established dog encounter defines only Skeleton Dog."
        "note.011.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.011.line.003.text" "The live deadlands roster is the explicit affected roster. Preserve existing ordinary-dog"
        "note.011.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.011.line.004.text" "selections elsewhere, dog encounter frequency and pack sizes. Each individual still rolls 99%"
        "note.011.line.005.state" "text"
        "note.011.line.005.text" "ordinary / 1% skeletal; do not add unrestricted Skeleton Dog spawns or new dog locations."
        "note.011.line.006.state" "text"
        "note.011.line.006.text" "Collie's existing traits, including its untameable dungeon-patrol exception, remain unchanged."
        "note.011.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.011.source.start" "483"
        "note.011.source.end" "488"
        "note.012.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.012.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.012.line.001.text" "**Owner amendment:** Skeleton Dog is **non-aggressive and tameable**, superseding its former"
        "note.012.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.012.line.002.text" "hostile/untameable policy. Items 8–9 below clarify normal dog behavior and taming food."
        "note.012.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.012.line.003.text" "Existing general taming eligibility restrictions and settlement protection remain; no riding"
        "note.012.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.012.line.004.text" "permission, numerical source ID, combat/loot bonus or other species-trait change is granted."
        "note.012.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.012.source.start" "490"
        "note.012.source.end" "493"
        "note.013.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.013.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.013.line.001.text" "**Hybrid family item 8 (owner clarified, 2026-09-27):** Skeleton Dog is a different dog breed,"
        "note.013.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.013.line.002.text" "not a special behavior category. It follows **normal dog behavior in the same encounter and"
        "note.013.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.013.line.003.text" "state**, including ordinary aggression/retaliation, pack response and taming reactions. Item 7's"
        "note.013.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.013.line.004.text" "non-aggression means the ordinary dog's baseline, not unconditional passivity overriding normal"
        "note.013.line.005.state" "text"
        "note.013.line.005.text" "encounter/provocation rules. The proposed Skeleton-Dog-only immunity to retaliation and to the"
        "note.013.line.006.state" "text"
        "note.013.line.006.text" "usual taming-induced group hostility is not adopted. Once tamed, normal pet behavior applies."
        "note.013.line.007.state" "text"
        "note.013.line.007.text" "The stable species ID, primary `dogs` family, descriptive memberships and independent `undead`"
        "note.013.line.008.state" "text"
        "note.013.line.008.text" "category remain; “dog race” does not introduce a playable `race` or new species-trait inheritance."
        "note.013.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.013.source.start" "495"
        "note.013.source.end" "502"
        "note.014.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.014.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.014.line.001.text" "**Hybrid family item 9 (owner approved, 2026-09-27):** the same **Bubble Gum (`bubble-gum`)**"
        "note.014.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.014.line.002.text" "tames both Collie and Skeleton Dog, under their ordinary eligibility rules. Keep Bubble Gum's"
        "note.014.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.014.line.003.text" "existing availability and prices; add no food, recipe or family-wide bait inheritance."
        "note.014.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.014.line.004.text" "The shared-food/source-ID contract is in §3.4 `pet-food` / §5 `c-food-id`."
        "note.014.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.014.source.start" "504"
        "note.014.source.end" "507"
        "note.015.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.015.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.015.line.001.text" "Documentation only: live rosters/traits and Bubble Gum's single-species mapping still lack"
        "note.015.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.015.line.002.text" "these decisions. Migration, model/loader/validator support and runtime enforcement remain"
        "note.015.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.015.line.003.text" "separately deferred and unauthorized."
        "note.015.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.015.source.start" "509"
        "note.015.source.end" "511"
    }
}

