        "property.008.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "property.008.source.start" "552"
        "property.008.source.end" "552"
        "property.008.type.state" "absent-column"
        "property.008.i-e.state" "absent-column"
        "property.008.notes.state" "absent-column"
        "property.008.value.state" "text"
        "property.008.value.text" "wraith pursues longer; most drop chase eventually `?`"
        "property.009.name" "clones"
        "property.009.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "property.009.source.start" "553"
        "property.009.source.end" "553"
        "property.009.type.state" "absent-column"
        "property.009.i-e.state" "absent-column"
        "property.009.notes.state" "absent-column"
        "property.009.value.state" "text"
        "property.009.value.text" "some bosses/NPC mages summon doppelgangers"
        "property.010.name" "possession"
        "property.010.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "property.010.source.start" "554"
        "property.010.source.end" "554"
        "property.010.type.state" "absent-column"
        "property.010.i-e.state" "absent-column"
        "property.010.notes.state" "absent-column"
        "property.010.value.state" "text"
        "property.010.value.text" "S: demon portal randomly possesses NPCs in the land (bigger, red, tougher, respawn possessed)"
        "property.011.name" "simulation"
        "property.011.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "property.011.source.start" "555"
        "property.011.source.end" "555"
        "property.011.type.state" "absent-column"
        "property.011.i-e.state" "absent-column"
        "property.011.notes.state" "absent-column"
        "property.011.value.state" "text"
        "property.011.value.text" "hybrid: beyond `design.spawns.ai.sim-radius`, movement and attacks stay frozen (D16); threat decay and taunt expiry reflect elapsed gameplay time (approved 2026-09-27, below). Distance = nearest player once `multiplayer-mode` lands (single player: the one player)."
        "note.002.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.002.source.start" "543"
        "note.002.source.end" "555"
        "note.003.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.003.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.001.text" "Hybrid aggro rules (owner approved 2026-09-18/19 and 2026-09-27, documentation only; relation definitions in"
        "note.003.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.002.text" "§4, constraints `c-threat-pair` / `c-current-target` in §5):"
        "note.003.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.003.text" "- **Pack membership (owner approved 2026-09-27):** creatures generated together as one"
        "note.003.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.004.text" "  spawned pack belong to that group. Nearby packs do not merge merely because they share"
        "note.003.line.005.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.005.text" "  a species or faction. Membership concerns spawned individuals, not `creature` definitions."
        "note.003.line.006.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.006.text" "- **Pack response (owner approved 2026-09-27):** a hostile pack responds when a member"
        "note.003.line.007.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.007.text" "  detects a player. Damaging a neutral member provokes its combat-capable packmates against"
        "note.003.line.008.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.008.text" "  that aggressor, not uninvolved players. Friendly/passive creatures are excluded. Returning"
        "note.003.line.009.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.009.text" "  members finish their protected return rather than being pulled back into combat. Neutral"
        "note.003.line.010.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.010.text" "  provocation establishes aggressor-specific eligibility, not unconditional pursuit at zero"
        "note.003.line.011.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.011.text" "  threat without detection; taunt alone grants no lasting neutral eligibility (below)."
        "note.003.line.012.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.012.text" "- **Shared awareness (owner approved 2026-09-27):** packmates share current sightings, not"
        "note.003.line.013.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.013.text" "  threat points or engagement order. Detection in these targeting rules includes a packmate's"
        "note.003.line.014.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.014.text" "  current sighting, so a member can react around a corner while another detects the player."
        "note.003.line.015.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.015.text" "  Once nobody in the pack detects that player, there is no retained shared sighting; each mob's"
        "note.003.line.016.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.016.text" "  own remaining threat governs continued pursuit. Apply targeting priorities independently per"
        "note.003.line.017.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.017.text" "  mob, preserving hostility/provocation eligibility and each member's protected return."
        "note.003.line.018.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.018.text" "- **Damage contribution (owner correction, 2026-09-18):** add **1 aggro point per 1% of the"
        "note.003.line.019.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.019.text" "  mob's maximum HP actually removed** by the attacker: `aggro gained = 100 × HP removed / mob max HP`."
        "note.003.line.020.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.020.text" "  Except at full stealth (below), use actual HP loss after reduction/absorption, not attempted"
        "note.003.line.021.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.021.text" "  damage; zero HP loss adds none."
        "note.003.line.022.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.022.text" "  Preserve fractional points (0.5% HP loss adds 0.5 points). Equal percentages generate equal"
        "note.003.line.023.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.023.text" "  threat at every progression level, so fixed-rate decay does not last longer just because"
        "note.003.line.024.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.024.text" "  HP/damage numbers are larger. This supersedes the raw-HP conversion, not the targeting rules."
        "note.003.line.025.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.025.text" "- **Full stealth (owner approved 2026-09-27):** full stealth prevents new damage-generated"
        "note.003.line.026.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.026.text" "  threat; it neither erases existing threat nor cancels an active taunt. Check the attacker's"
        "note.003.line.027.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.027.text" "  stealth when damage lands, before that hit consumes the stealth bar; check each damage-over-time"
        "note.003.line.028.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.028.text" "  tick individually. Camouflage can sustain threat-free damage while it keeps stealth full."
        "note.003.line.029.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.029.text" "  Partial stealth retains its existing detection-range reduction, with no additional threat"
        "note.003.line.030.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.030.text" "  multiplier. Existing positive threat can still sustain pursuit; ordinary zero-threat targeting"
        "note.003.line.031.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.031.text" "  still requires detection. Stealth is not automatic rescue for an existing target, but can allow"
        "note.003.line.032.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.032.text" "  attacks without pulling an enemy that cannot detect the attacker."
        "note.003.line.033.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.033.text" "- **Current-target ties:** during ordinary threat-based targeting, retain the current target"
        "note.003.line.034.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.034.text" "  when tied for highest threat. Another attacker must exceed it to displace it through threat"
        "note.003.line.035.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.035.text" "  alone; equal scores do not cause arbitrary switching."
        "note.003.line.036.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.036.text" "- **Other-target ties:** when the highest threat is positive and the current target is not"
        "note.003.line.037.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.037.text" "  among the highest-threat attackers, choose the tied leader who engaged that enemy first,"
        "note.003.line.038.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.038.text" "  not the nearest or latest hitter, nor randomly. Higher threat and current-target retention"
        "note.003.line.039.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.039.text" "  take precedence over engagement order; zero-threat fallback is defined below."
        "note.003.line.040.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.040.text" "- **Zero-threat fallback (owner approved 2026-09-19):** in ordinary targeting, when no eligible"
        "note.003.line.041.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.041.text" "  positive-threat player takes priority and there is no valid current target, choose the nearest"
        "note.003.line.042.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.042.text" "  eligible player among those the mob normally detects. This does not generate aggro or assign an"
        "note.003.line.043.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.043.text" "  engagement-order position. Retaining a valid current target tied for highest threat still"
        "note.003.line.044.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.044.text" "  takes precedence: a closer zero-threat player does not displace it. **Exact-distance ties"
        "note.003.line.045.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.045.text" "  (owner approved 2026-09-27):** choose once at random with equal chances among equally nearest"
        "note.003.line.046.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.046.text" "  detected players, then retain that target under the existing tie rule; do not repeatedly reroll."
        "note.003.line.047.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.047.text" "- **Heroic Shout (owner approved 2026-09-27):** affected enemies must target the caster"
        "note.003.line.048.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.048.text" "  for **3 seconds**, overriding ordinary threat priority without adding or copying aggro points"
        "note.003.line.049.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.049.text" "  or assigning engagement order. Damage gains and decay continue underneath. On expiry, resume"
        "note.003.line.050.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.050.text" "  ordinary targeting, including retention of a valid tied current target; lasting control is"
        "note.003.line.051.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.051.text" "  not guaranteed. Preserve the existing **5-metre radius**, healing (50% max HP over 10 seconds),"
        "note.003.line.052.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.052.text" "  30-second base cooldown and existing skill-point scaling; this adds no taunt-duration scaling."
        "note.003.line.053.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.053.text" "- **Neutral eligibility after taunt (follow-up 14, owner approved 2026-09-27):** taunt alone"
        "note.003.line.054.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.054.text" "  adds no neutral provocation or lasting ordinary eligibility for a previously uninvolved caster."
        "note.003.line.055.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.055.text" "  When it expires, reconsider legitimate aggressors under ordinary targeting and detection rules;"
        "note.003.line.056.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.056.text" "  return home if no eligible target remains. A tied current target is retained only if ordinarily"
        "note.003.line.057.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.057.text" "  eligible, not merely because it was forced by taunt. For example, A damages a neutral pack and"
        "note.003.line.058.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.058.text" "  B only taunts: at expiry with all scores zero, reconsider A if detected, not B merely for taunting."
        "note.003.line.059.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.059.text" "  If B damages the pack, the existing aggressor-specific pack-provocation rule applies."
        "note.003.line.060.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.060.text" "- **Taunt eligibility (owner approved 2026-09-27):** Heroic Shout affects hostile enemies"
        "note.003.line.061.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.061.text" "  and already-provoked neutral enemies within 5 metres, including through cover; walls do not"
        "note.003.line.062.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.062.text" "  block application. It does not provoke peaceful neutrals or affect friendly/passive creatures."
        "note.003.line.063.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.063.text" "- **Competing taunts (owner approved 2026-09-27):** the latest successful taunt replaces the"
        "note.003.line.064.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.064.text" "  previous one and starts its own duration; replaced taunts never resume. For genuinely"
        "note.003.line.065.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.065.text" "  simultaneous taunts, choose one caster randomly once. **Winner scope (follow-up 13, owner"
        "note.003.line.066.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.066.text" "  approved 2026-09-27):** each affected enemy chooses independently among simultaneous eligible"
        "note.003.line.067.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.067.text" "  taunters whose casts reached that enemy. A pack may split between casters; there is no shared"
        "note.003.line.068.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.068.text" "  winner or guarantee of keeping the pack together."
        "note.003.line.069.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.069.text" "- **Taunt termination (owner approved 2026-09-27):** starting return cancels any active taunt;"
        "note.003.line.070.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.070.text" "  new taunts cannot interrupt protected return or queue for afterward. Outside return, a taunt"
        "note.003.line.071.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.071.text" "  ends early if its caster dies or disappears. Moving beyond the initial 5-metre casting radius"
        "note.003.line.072.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.072.text" "  alone does not cancel it; the existing home leash still applies."
        "note.003.line.073.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.073.text" "- **Continuous decay (rate approved 2026-09-18):** each mob tracks each player's threat"
        "note.003.line.074.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.074.text" "  separately and subtracts **1 aggro point per elapsed second**, both while fighting and while"
        "note.003.line.075.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.075.text" "  not fighting. Decay is continuous (0.5 seconds removes 0.5 points), not whole-second ticks."
        "note.003.line.076.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.076.text" "  Hits keep adding their normal damage-based threat while decay continues; attacking does not"
        "note.003.line.077.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.077.text" "  pause or restart the countdown."
        "note.003.line.078.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.078.text" "- **Distant timers (owner approved 2026-09-27):** threat decay and taunt expiry use elapsed"
        "note.003.line.079.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.079.text" "  gameplay time even while the mob is outside the simulation radius. On reactivation, remaining"
        "note.003.line.080.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.080.text" "  threat and taunt duration reflect the time that passed; movement and attacks remain frozen"
        "note.003.line.081.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.081.text" "  while distant. This approval does not extend to every other status timer or choose how to"
        "note.003.line.082.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.082.text" "  implement elapsed-time accounting."
        "note.003.line.083.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.083.text" "- **Retained threat:** switching targets does not clear other players' remaining threat. If the"
        "note.003.line.084.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.084.text" "  higher-threat teammate dies, a player with remaining positive threat can be targeted again"
        "note.003.line.085.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.085.text" "  according to the normal highest-threat/tie rules; losing priority is not being \"forgiven\"."
        "note.003.line.086.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.086.text" "- **Zero threat (approved 2026-09-18):** decay stops at zero, never going negative. At zero,"
        "note.003.line.087.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.087.text" "  past hits alone no longer justify ordinary pursuit of that player; there is no separate damage"
        "note.003.line.088.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.088.text" "  memory extending it. Without an active taunt, if the mob no longer detects that player, it stops"
        "note.003.line.089.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.089.text" "  pursuing them. Normal detection of an eligible player (hostile or provoked-neutral rules) can"
        "note.003.line.090.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.090.text" "  still start or maintain aggression at zero; reaching zero is not immunity."
        "note.003.line.091.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.091.text" "  Other players' remaining threat is unchanged; full stealth does not erase it."
        "note.003.line.092.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.092.text" "- **Zero-threat tie-breaker memory (owner correction, 2026-09-19):** when a mob's aggro toward"
        "note.003.line.093.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.093.text" "  a player reaches zero, discard that player's remembered engagement-order position for that"
        "note.003.line.094.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.094.text" "  mob. Do not retain or restore pre-zero tie-breaking priority. Other players' scores and order"
        "note.003.line.095.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.095.text" "  are unchanged. Normal hostile detection, higher-threat priority and current-target tie"
        "note.003.line.096.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.096.text" "  retention still apply; clearing historical order does not force a target switch."
        "note.003.line.097.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.097.text" "- **Fresh engagement order (owner approved 2026-09-19):** after reaching zero, assign a new"
        "note.003.line.098.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.098.text" "  engagement-order position when that player's aggro toward that mob next rises above zero,"
        "note.003.line.099.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.099.text" "  after players whose existing positions remain valid. Under the approved damage rule, this"
        "note.003.line.100.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.100.text" "  requires damage that generates positive aggro, not proximity, detection or a missed attack."
        "note.003.line.101.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.101.text" "  Higher threat and current-target tie retention still take precedence. Zero-threat fallback"
        "note.003.line.102.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.102.text" "  does not assign an engagement-order position, nor does taunting."
        "note.003.line.103.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.103.text" "- **Player death (approved 2026-09-19):** death immediately clears every mob's aggro points"
        "note.003.line.104.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.104.text" "  toward that player, without changing surviving teammates' scores or their normal decay."
        "note.003.line.105.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.105.text" "  After respawn, the player rebuilds aggro from zero; normal hostile detection still applies."
        "note.003.line.106.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.106.text" "  Death also clears that player's engagement-order position with every mob. Fresh assignment"
        "note.003.line.107.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.107.text" "  follows the rule above; surviving teammates keep their positions. Higher aggro and current-target"
        "note.003.line.108.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.108.text" "  retention still take precedence."
        "note.003.line.109.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.109.text" "- **Escape (owner approved 2026-09-19):** getting away or ending pursuit alone does not clear"
        "note.003.line.110.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.110.text" "  that player's remaining positive aggro or engagement-order position with the mob. Normal decay"
        "note.003.line.111.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.111.text" "  continues; reaching zero clears the old position, and regaining positive threat assigns a fresh"
        "note.003.line.112.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.112.text" "  one as above. Other players' scores and order are unchanged. This governs memory, not chase distance."
        "note.003.line.113.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.113.text" "- **Temporary absence (owner approved 2026-09-27):** within the same running world,"
        "note.003.line.114.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.114.text" "  temporary player disconnect or zone unloading does not grant an extra threat/order wipe."
        "note.003.line.115.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.115.text" "  Preserve the logical mob/player pair's remaining state under normal decay and approved resets;"
        "note.003.line.116.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.116.text" "  an absent player cannot be targeted. Reconnecting before threat expires can restore eligibility"
        "note.003.line.117.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.117.text" "  under normal targeting rules, not guaranteed priority. A mob that actually dies and respawns"
        "note.003.line.118.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.118.text" "  starts with fresh threat/order. Restart retention follows persistence item 9 below;"
        "note.003.line.119.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.119.text" "  neither decision chooses a storage strategy."
        "note.003.line.120.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.120.text" "- **Restart persistence (hybrid persistence item 9, owner approved 2026-09-28):** save each"
        "note.003.line.121.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.121.text" "  **surviving logical mob's remaining threat, engagement order and neutral provocation** across"
        "note.003.line.122.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.122.text" "  a server restart. Restarting alone grants no wipe; shutdown downtime causes no decay under"
        "note.003.line.123.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.123.text" "  `game-clock` persistence item 8. Resume normal targeting and return-home rules: absent players"
        "note.003.line.124.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.124.text" "  cannot be targeted, and caster disappearance still terminates taunts. Each mob/player pair"
        "note.003.line.125.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.125.text" "  remains independent; normal gains/decay and the approved zero, player-death and home-arrival"
        "note.003.line.126.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.126.text" "  resets still apply. Actual mob death/respawn starts fresh, not from the saved survivor record."
        "note.003.line.127.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.127.text" "  For example, saved threat of 10 resumes at 10, then ordinary decay or completed return can"
        "note.003.line.128.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.128.text" "  clear it. This promises no full combat snapshot, resurrected target node, guaranteed target"
        "note.003.line.129.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.129.text" "  priority, resumed expired/terminated taunt or unrelated HP/status/cooldown persistence."
        "note.003.line.130.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.130.text" "- **Return-home trigger (owner approved 2026-09-19):** during pursuit, crossing the existing"
        "note.003.line.131.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.131.text" "  home leash (`design.spawns.ai.leash`, 30 blocks measured from the mob's home) starts return"
        "note.003.line.132.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.132.text" "  regardless of remaining aggro or taunt. Within the leash, if its target dies, disappears, or"
        "note.003.line.133.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.133.text" "  (outside an active taunt) has zero aggro and is no longer detected, first consider other living"
        "note.003.line.134.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.134.text" "  eligible players with positive aggro using the approved highest-threat/tie rules. If none"
        "note.003.line.135.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.135.text" "  remain, normal detection of eligible players can still sustain combat; otherwise return home."
        "note.003.line.136.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.136.text" "  Starting return does not clear aggro or engagement order; normal decay continues. Protected return and the arrival reset follow below."
        "note.003.line.137.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.137.text" "- **Protected return (owner approved 2026-09-19):** attacks do not restart pursuit once the"
        "note.003.line.138.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.138.text" "  mob is returning, including after it moves back inside the home leash. During return, its"
        "note.003.line.139.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.139.text" "  movement speed is **×2 the normal return speed** (currently `design.spawns.ai.chase`: 6.5 →"
        "note.003.line.140.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.140.text" "  **13 blocks/s**), and damage it would otherwise receive is reduced by **90%** (it takes 10%),"
        "note.003.line.141.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.141.text" "  including poison and burning ticks. These temporary return-state modifiers do not change"
        "note.003.line.142.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.142.text" "  ordinary chase speed or define the general resistance stat. Existing status effects still"
        "note.003.line.143.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.143.text" "  apply; no status cleansing or crowd-control immunity is granted."
        "note.003.line.144.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.144.text" "  On reaching home alive, restore **full HP once** and end the return-speed/damage-reduction"
        "note.003.line.145.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.145.text" "  bonuses. A mob killed before arrival stays dead. Aggro follows the existing gain/decay rules"
        "note.003.line.146.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.146.text" "  during return; taunts cannot interrupt it (taunt termination above)."
        "note.003.line.147.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.147.text" "  This discourages repeated damage during retreat but does not make retreat kills impossible."
        "note.003.line.148.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.148.text" "- **Arrival aggro/order reset (owner approved 2026-09-19):** on completing return home alive,"
        "note.003.line.149.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.149.text" "  clear that mob's remaining aggro points and engagement-order positions toward **every player**,"
        "note.003.line.150.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.150.text" "  once, alongside its full-HP recovery. During the journey, gains and decay continue normally;"
        "note.003.line.151.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.151.text" "  starting return is not a wipe. Other mobs' threat/order records are unchanged. Normal hostile"
        "note.003.line.152.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.152.text" "  detection and existing targeting priorities still apply; zero aggro grants no immunity."
        "note.003.line.153.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.153.text" "  Damage after arrival builds fresh aggro and order normally, including subsequent poison/burning"
        "note.003.line.154.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.154.text" "  ticks, because arrival does not cleanse statuses."
        "note.003.line.155.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.155.text" "- **Neutral forgiveness (owner approved 2026-09-27):** completing return home also clears"
        "note.003.line.156.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.156.text" "  that creature's provocation toward every aggressor. It becomes peaceful again; merely seeing"
        "note.003.line.157.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.157.text" "  the previous aggressor, directly or via pack awareness, cannot re-provoke it. A new damaging"
        "note.003.line.158.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.158.text" "  attack can provoke it again under the pack-response rule. Arrival is individual: it does not"
        "note.003.line.159.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.159.text" "  clear other packmates' provocation, threat or engagement order."
        "note.003.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.003.source.start" "557"
        "note.003.source.end" "715"
        "note.004.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.004.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.004.line.001.text" "Remaining uncertainties are indexed in §7; deferred application is tracked in"
        "note.004.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.004.line.002.text" "`docs/ROADMAP/todo_implement.md`."
        "note.004.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.004.line.003.text" "These documentation decisions do not authorize runtime or live-data changes."
        "note.004.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.004.source.start" "717"
        "note.004.source.end" "719"
        "note.005.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.005.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.005.line.001.text" "Hybrid (D26): `combat-role` mapping is defined under [creature (locator=creature)](3_Classes.dsl), with resolution per"
        "note.005.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.005.line.002.text" "spawned group in §6 `gen-spawns`; melee retains its reach attack. Ranged / mage chase to a `range`,"
        "note.005.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.005.line.003.text" "back off below a `keep-away` distance, need line of sight,"
        "note.005.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.005.line.004.text" "then wind up and fire a projectile (`design.creature-roles`, keyed by role and overridable per species — spitter,"
        "note.005.line.005.state" "text"
        "note.005.line.005.text" "snout-beetle) that damages through the target's normal dodge / block / i-frames and rolls its `applies` statuses on a"
        "note.005.line.006.state" "text"
        "note.005.line.006.text" "landed hit, with normal D23 enemy-hit stun/knockback rolls ([status-effect (locator=status-effect)](3_Classes.dsl))."
        "note.005.line.007.state" "text"
        "note.005.line.007.text" "Poison is never avoided by dodge. A creature shot never damages another creature."
        "note.005.line.008.state" "text"
        "note.005.line.008.text" "`c-creature-roles`."
        "note.005.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.005.source.start" "721"
        "note.005.source.end" "728"
        "note.006.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.006.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.006.line.001.text" "Aggro tables/group response, enemy combos/potions, Wizard laser/Witch ray beams, any-class humanoid"
        "note.006.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.006.line.002.text" "class/equipment/appearance, Snout Beetle dodge and pathfinding are outside the D26 slice, not final bans;"
        "note.006.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.006.line.003.text" "the approved AI rules above still govern the target."
        "note.006.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.006.source.start" "730"
        "note.006.source.end" "732"
    }
}

r_mob_strength_tier = element "mob-strength-tier" "Class" {
    tags "Class,Entities"
    properties {
        "id" "mob-strength-tier"
        "kind" "Class"
        "order" "734"
        "source.commit" "175e0c59b6a05ead62d29bd851085cd5a3818378"
        "source.status" "historical baseline coordinates"
        "source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "source.start" "734"
        "source.end" "738"
        "title" "mob-strength-tier"
        "heading.level" "3"
        "heading.slug" "mob-strength-tier"
        "section" "Entities"
        "note.001.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.001.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.001.text" "S enemy power colour: white (150–250 HP, farm animals) < green < blue < purple (dungeon base) <"
        "note.001.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.002.text" "yellow (legendary; minotaurs, some collies). A equivalents: land level + `+1..+4` multiplier"
        "note.001.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.003.text" "and boss tag; landmark name colour white/blue/red vs player. → `instances/rarities.json#tiers`."
        "note.001.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.001.source.start" "735"
        "note.001.source.end" "737"
    }
}

