r_equipment_slot = element "equipment-slot" "Class" {
    tags "Class,Items"
    properties {
        "id" "equipment-slot"
        "kind" "Class"
        "order" "1021"
        "source.commit" "175e0c59b6a05ead62d29bd851085cd5a3818378"
        "source.status" "historical baseline coordinates"
        "source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "source.start" "1021"
        "source.end" "1051"
        "title" "equipment-slot"
        "heading.level" "3"
        "heading.slug" "equipment-slot"
        "section" "Items"
        "note.001.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.001.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.001.text" "13 indexed entity storage positions, including reserved `unknown-0` (not usable). The 12 usable"
        "note.001.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.002.text" "positions are amulet, chest, gloves, boots, shoulders, main-hand, off-hand, ring-left, ring-right,"
        "note.001.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.003.text" "lamp, special and pet. Preserve every index in `instances/equipment-slots.json`; no extra slot"
        "note.001.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.004.text" "or stat bonus is added. The [quick consumable (locator=quick-item)](controls.dsl) is separate: selecting it does not displace gear."
        "note.001.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.001.source.start" "1022"
        "note.001.source.end" "1025"
        "note.002.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.002.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.001.text" "Approved hybrid model (reconciliation item 3, 2026-09-15): `accepts` names `item-type` IDs,"
        "note.002.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.002.text" "with subtype restrictions where needed:"
        "note.002.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.003.text" "- `lamp` accepts `light` (subtype `lamp`)."
        "note.002.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.004.text" "- `special` accepts `special` (subtypes `hang-glider` or `boat`), one equipped at a time."
        "note.002.line.005.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.005.text" "- Hand slots accept `weapon`; shields are weapon subtypes, not a separate item type."
        "note.002.line.006.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.006.text" "  Existing class and handedness restrictions still apply (`c-weapon-class`, `c-hands`)."
        "note.002.line.007.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.007.text" "- `pet` accepts a `pet-cage` or `pet-food` during taming, without replacing the quick-consumable selection."
        "note.002.line.008.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.008.text" "- Armor and jewelry retain their matching slots; `unknown-0` accepts nothing."
        "note.002.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.002.source.start" "1027"
        "note.002.source.end" "1034"
        "note.003.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.003.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.001.text" "The item-3 slot-model approval is ontology-only: normalizing live slot JSON and its consumers"
        "note.003.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.002.text" "awaits separate authorization (`docs/ROADMAP/todo_implement.md`). Wand handedness is approved"
        "note.003.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.003.text" "under `weapon-type`; traversal approvals are recorded separately under `skill-tree` / `pet`."
        "note.003.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.004.text" "Gliding/sailing require the respective Hang Glider/Boat equipped in `special`, not merely bought"
        "note.003.line.005.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.005.text" "(traversal items 2–3, approved 2026-09-28). They share that single slot; no dual equip or new slot."
        "note.003.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.003.source.start" "1036"
        "note.003.source.end" "1040"
        "note.004.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.004.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.004.line.001.text" "Hybrid hand-conflict repair (item 10, authorized 2026-09-17): reject an equip attempt that would"
        "note.004.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.004.line.002.text" "pair a two-handed weapon with a shield, regardless of equip order. Leave existing equipment and"
        "note.004.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.004.line.003.text" "the attempted item in the bag unchanged; do not auto-unequip, delete or duplicate either item."
        "note.004.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.004.line.004.text" "The repair uses loaded handedness classifications without changing them; it did not settle the"
        "note.004.line.005.state" "text"
        "note.004.line.005.text" "then-provisional wand classification. The later Wand item 1 rule is recorded under `weapon-type`;"
        "note.004.line.006.state" "text"
        "note.004.line.006.text" "its live-data migration remains deferred. Valid one-handed-plus-shield setups, two-handed weapons"
        "note.004.line.007.state" "text"
        "note.004.line.007.text" "alone and non-conflicting slot replacements keep working. This authorizes only the conflict"
        "note.004.line.008.state" "text"
        "note.004.line.008.text" "repair and regressions, not the broader slot model, class restrictions, dual-wield routing,"
        "note.004.line.009.state" "text"
        "note.004.line.009.text" "Guardian/Cyclone blocking changes, or the later Wand item 1 migration."
        "note.004.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.004.source.start" "1042"
        "note.004.source.end" "1050"
    }
}

