        "source.start" "1413"
        "source.end" "1416"
        "title" "control-action"
        "heading.level" "3"
        "heading.slug" "control-action"
        "section" "Meta"
        "note.001.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.001.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.001.text" "A distinct device-independent player intention: stable ID, meaning, value/lifecycle, context"
        "note.001.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.002.text" "and effect reference. Defined once in [controls](controls.dsl), not inferred from a shared input."
        "note.001.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.001.source.start" "1414"
        "note.001.source.end" "1415"
    }
}

r_controller_profile = element "controller-profile" "Class" {
    tags "Class,Meta"
    properties {
        "id" "controller-profile"
        "kind" "Class"
        "order" "1417"
        "source.commit" "175e0c59b6a05ead62d29bd851085cd5a3818378"
        "source.status" "historical baseline coordinates"
        "source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "source.start" "1417"
        "source.end" "1422"
        "title" "controller-profile"
        "heading.level" "3"
        "heading.slug" "controller-profile"
        "section" "Meta"
        "note.001.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.001.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.001.text" "Device-specific bindings and their mapping status, aliases and contextual input shapes."
        "note.001.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.002.text" "[Profiles](controller-profiles.dsl) refer to canonical actions; keyboard/mouse is documented,"
        "note.001.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.003.text" "gamepad remains unselected, and Android's [native tool stack](../decisions/android-native-touch-controls.md)"
        "note.001.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.004.text" "and [touch-profile policy (locator=android)](controller-profiles.dsl) have a bounded first-slice runtime, owner hardware-tested; detailed coverage and render cost remain unrecorded."
        "note.001.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.001.source.start" "1418"
        "note.001.source.end" "1421"
    }
}

r_input_binding = element "input-binding" "Class" {
    tags "Class,Meta"
    properties {
        "id" "input-binding"
        "kind" "Class"
        "order" "1423"
        "source.commit" "175e0c59b6a05ead62d29bd851085cd5a3818378"
        "source.status" "historical baseline coordinates"
        "source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "source.start" "1423"
        "source.end" "1429"
        "title" "input-binding"
        "heading.level" "3"
        "heading.slug" "input-binding"
        "section" "Meta"
        "note.001.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.001.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.001.text" "A physical input/shape in a controller profile referring to one or more distinct control actions."
        "note.001.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.002.text" "Several bindings may invoke one action; one input may serve several actions with documented"
        "note.001.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.003.text" "phases/context, without merging their meanings. Current executable keyboard adapter:"
        "note.001.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.004.text" "`instances/keybinds.json#hybrid`; its [profile (locator=keyboard-and-mouse)](controller-profiles.dsl)"
        "note.001.line.005.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.005.text" "explains legacy grouping, aliases and implementation gaps. Remapping/persistence is deferred."
        "note.001.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.001.source.start" "1424"
        "note.001.source.end" "1428"
    }
}

r_hud_element = element "hud-element" "Class" {
    tags "Class,Meta"
    properties {
        "id" "hud-element"
        "kind" "Class"
        "order" "1430"
        "source.commit" "175e0c59b6a05ead62d29bd851085cd5a3818378"
        "source.status" "historical baseline coordinates"
        "source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "source.start" "1430"
        "source.end" "1456"
        "title" "hud-element"
        "heading.level" "3"
        "heading.slug" "hud-element"
        "section" "Meta"
        "note.001.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.001.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.001.text" "→ `instances/ui.json`: portrait+name+level/class+HP+XP (A), coins + key-item bar (S), HP/MP/stamina"
        "note.001.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.002.text" "bars, hotbar ([basic (locator=basic-attack)](controls.dsl), [special (locator=special-attack)](controls.dsl), class slots and [quick item (locator=quick-item)](controls.dsl)), stealth bar, pet HP/XP/hydration, message log, minimap (3-D,"
        "note.001.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.003.text" "rotating, scalable), compass, time/temperature/humidity, land caption, buff icons `S`, help widget"
        "note.001.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.004.text" "`S`, damage numbers, combo counter, stun stars, enemy name colours + stars, chat, world map (3-D"
        "note.001.line.005.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.005.text" "voxel, zoom 1:4..1:256, markers, missions, players, shrines, flight points), overview map `A`,"
        "note.001.line.006.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.006.text" "character sheet (power, HP, armor, resi, crit, haste, reg, weapon/armor rating), skills window `A`,"
        "note.001.line.007.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.007.text" "crafting window, inventory, quick-select wheel, customization bench UI, character creation, world"
        "note.001.line.008.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.008.text" "selection `A`, friends widget `S`. Hybrid (D17): `debug-menu` — the runtime profiling overlay any player"
        "note.001.line.009.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.009.text" "can open without a dev environment (Godot Debug Menu add-on: FPS, frametime, CPU/GPU graphs, GPU +"
        "note.001.line.010.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.010.text" "driver, OS; [debug-menu control (locator=debug-menu)](controls.dsl) cycles hidden/compact/full; shipped in release exports)."
        "note.001.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.001.source.start" "1431"
        "note.001.source.end" "1440"
        "note.002.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.002.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.001.text" "Hybrid (D25): floating target numbers, stars over stunned heads and buff icons with countdown fill"
        "note.002.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.002.text" "use `generators.json#design.feel`. The level-up toast pops from `level-up.pop-scale` back to ×1"
        "note.002.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.003.text" "over `level-up.pop-s`."
        "note.002.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.002.source.start" "1442"
        "note.002.source.end" "1444"
        "note.003.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.003.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.001.text" "Hybrid panel-time policy (walkthrough item 10, owner approved 2026-09-17): opening the inventory,"
        "note.003.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.002.text" "skill-tree or shop panel does not pause time, in either solo or multiplayer. The world and player"
        "note.003.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.003.text" "timers continue together: enemies and projectiles remain active, damage-over-time effects tick,"
        "note.003.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.004.text" "cooldowns count down, buffs expire and dodge protection ends under their existing rules. Opening"
        "note.003.line.005.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.005.text" "these panels grants no immunity or extension of protection; players remain vulnerable while browsing."
        "note.003.line.006.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.006.text" "This does not decide new input availability or the behavior of other panels/menus."
        "note.003.line.007.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.007.text" "Panel-time runtime authorization (walkthrough item 10, owner approved 2026-09-17): repair the"
        "note.003.line.008.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.008.text" "player-only timer freeze and add regressions for these three panels. Preserve current gameplay"
        "note.003.line.009.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.009.text" "input restrictions, balance and other menus; advance existing simulation rather than admitting"
        "note.003.line.010.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.010.text" "new movement, combat or interaction input. Other runtime fixes remain separately deferred."
        "note.003.source.file" "3_Classes.md"
        "note.003.source.start" "1446"
        "note.003.source.end" "1455"
    }
}

